diagnosis_text:
No fault found. The sshswitch Layer-3 SVIs for VLAN 5 and VLAN 6 are up and functioning. On sshswitch, the SVI interfaces are present and operational: br_v5 is UP with IP 10.5.0.254/24 and br_v6 is UP with IP 10.6.0.254/24 (ip addr shows both “UP, LOWER_UP”). Their associated VLAN subinterfaces (bond0.5/bond0.6 and eth0.5/eth0.6) are also UP and enslaved to the correct bridges.

Client reachability to the default gateways is confirmed:
- VLAN 5: pc1 (10.5.0.1), pc2 (10.5.0.2), and dc_pc5 (10.5.0.5) each ping 10.5.0.254 with 0% loss.
- VLAN 6: pc3 (10.6.0.3) and pc4 (10.6.0.4) each ping 10.6.0.254 with 0% loss.

On the access side, switch4 shows the expected VLAN trunking toward sshswitch: eth0.5 is in br_vlan5 and eth0.6 is in br_vlan6, indicating VLAN 5/6 are carried across the uplink. This corroborates end-to-end L2/L3 path health.

Mechanism: If users briefly observed loss after a reload, it may have been transient during interface/bridge reconvergence, but current evidence shows normal operation.

Root cause: No current outage; the reported “SVIs down” condition is not present.

Corrective fix: No action required. If issues reappear intermittently, consider capturing timestamps and checking the sshswitch bond/trunk status and ARP/bridge tables during the event, but at present the gateways are up and reachable. 
=== END ===